Exposure: `limited_exposure_with_choices`. Germany is non-nuclear, but Scholz in 2022 still had real existential-risk choices through NATO nuclear sharing, arms-control diplomacy, crisis rhetoric, and alliance coordination. I did not use the client matrix or re-fetch the local structured priors.

**Reused evidence**
None.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Olaf Scholz (2021 - 2025)","publisher":"Federal Chancellor","publication_date":"live page (accessed 2026-07-22)","url":"https://www.bundeskanzler.de/bk-en/chancellorship-olaf-scholz-2344810","claim":"Scholz was elected federal chancellor in December 2021 and led the first SPD-Greens-FDP federal coalition; the page frames 2022 as the moment Russia's war triggered a major security rupture.","locator":"biography section, lines 176-180 in the opened page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government biography; strong for office, coalition, and period framing, though self-presenting.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited baseline and 2022 office context.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Scholz's office and coalition baseline; not a claim about personal performance.","contrary_evidence":["Self-description is not independent evaluation.","Later retrospective framing can compress the 2022 chronology."],"lenses":["1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Tasks of the Chancellor","publisher":"Federal Chancellor","publication_date":"live page (accessed 2026-07-22)","url":"https://www.bundeskanzler.de/bk-de/kanzleramt/aufgaben-des-bundeskanzlers","claim":"The chancellor sets policy guidelines, chairs cabinet, and carries overall responsibility, but coalition agreements and ministerial autonomy constrain how that authority is exercised.","locator":"lines 172-200 in the opened page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official institutional explainer for executive authority and coalition constraints.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct institutional context for the 2022 chancellorship.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Scholz's actual office; the limits are structural rather than personal.","contrary_evidence":["Explains formal authority, not how much was used effectively in 2022.","Government framing may understate coalition friction."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Grundgesetz Art. 65","publisher":"Gesetze im Internet","publication_date":"live law page (accessed 2026-07-22)","url":"https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/gg/art_65.html","claim":"Article 65 gives the chancellor the right to set policy guidelines and places day-to-day ministerial responsibility within those guidelines with the federal ministers.","locator":"Article 65, first sentence and surrounding text","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary constitutional text; strongest source for the legal scope of the office.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Stable legal baseline for Scholz's 2022 authority.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the office Scholz held; not a performance judgment.","contrary_evidence":["Formal legal power does not equal practical control over coalition bargaining.","Does not capture Bundestag or coalition veto points."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Election of the Federal Chancellor","publisher":"German Bundestag","publication_date":"live page (accessed 2026-07-22)","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/en/parliament/function/chancellor","claim":"The Bundestag elects the chancellor by absolute majority, and removal is only possible through a constructive vote of no confidence that also names a successor.","locator":"lines 399-403 in the opened page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary procedure page; strong for constraints on chancellor power.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to Scholz's coalition-dependent authority in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Structural constraint on Scholz's governing power rather than a personal act.","contrary_evidence":["Describes formal removal mechanics, not informal coalition discipline.","Does not address emergency decision-making inside NATO."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Germany's Scholz warns Russia over Ukraine, but says 'we want peace'","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-02-11","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/02/11/us-ukraine-crisis-germany-baltic","claim":"Before the invasion, Scholz warned Russia of serious political, economic, and strategic consequences if it escalated against Ukraine, while also saying Germany and its allies were ready for dialogue and wanted peace.","locator":"lead paragraph and article summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting via a reputable outlet; strong contemporaneous coverage of Scholz's prewar posture.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate pre-invasion crisis context in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz conduct and messaging; attributable to the ruler, not inherited policy.","contrary_evidence":["Warnings are not the same as concrete risk-reduction measures.","The source is a mediated Reuters report, not a transcript."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Policy statement by Olaf Scholz, Chancellor of the Federal Republic of Germany, 27 February 2022 in Berlin","publisher":"Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-en/service/archive/policy-statement-by-olaf-scholz-chancellor-of-the-federal-republic-of-germany-and-member-of-the-german-bundestag-27-february-2022-in-berlin-2008378","claim":"Scholz tied Germany's response to the Ukraine invasion to a modern replacement for the Tornado jets for nuclear sharing, while also calling for stronger resilience against cyberattacks, disinformation, and attacks on critical infrastructure.","locator":"lines 346-362 in the opened page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government speech; excellent for dated policy commitments and ruler attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period and central to 2022 security policy.","ruler_attribution":"Scholz personally announced the policy direction, though implementation depended on cabinet and allies.","contrary_evidence":["Speech gives intent and framing, not implementation or outcomes.","Official rhetoric may emphasize resolve over delay or dissent."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Berlin wants to buy 35 Lockheed F-35 fighter jets, def min tells parliament","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-14","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/berlin-wants-to-buy-35-lockheed-f35-fighter-jets-def-min-tells-parliament-2784052","claim":"Germany moved to buy 35 F-35 fighters to replace its ageing Tornado aircraft in the nuclear-sharing role, marking a concrete follow-through on the February shift.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with a clear dated procurement decision; strong corroboration of the chancellor's policy line.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tightly tied to the nuclear-sharing posture.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Scholz's government and security policy direction, even though the defense minister announced the operational step.","contrary_evidence":["Procurement is an implementation step, not a full command-and-control reform.","The aircraft are for nuclear sharing, not independent German nuclear capability."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.6","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Olaf Scholz: \"There will be no direct military involvement in the war\"","publisher":"DIE ZEIT","publication_date":"2022-03","url":"https://www.zeit.de/politik/deutschland/2022-03/olaf-scholz-ukraine-russia-sanction-english/seite-2","claim":"Scholz said Germany would not enter the war directly and rejected a no-fly zone because it would risk direct conflict between NATO and Russia.","locator":"lines 121, 129-130 in the opened page","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct interview transcript with Scholz in a major independent outlet; strong for rhetoric and escalation restraint.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period and central to crisis de-escalation choices.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz choice and articulation of escalation boundaries.","contrary_evidence":["A no-fly-zone refusal is a restraint choice, but it also reflects alliance limits and caution.","Does not by itself prove broader arms-control leadership."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Non-Proliferation and Disarmament Initiative - 11th High-level Meeting Joint High-level Statement","publisher":"Federal Foreign Office","publication_date":"2022-08-01","url":"https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/newsroom/news/2546078-2546078","claim":"Germany, through the NPDI, endorsed transparency, NPT-strengthening, disarmament verification, nuclear risk reduction, and better nuclear safety, security, and safeguards.","locator":"paragraph 13 and surrounding text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary multilateral statement naming Germany as a participant and specifying risk-reduction goals.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and highly relevant to arms-control posture.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to the German government under Scholz, though delivered through the NPDI and foreign ministry channels.","contrary_evidence":["Multilateral statements can be aspirational and not implementation evidence.","The source does not isolate Scholz's personal role in drafting."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.7","1B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement of the G7 Non-Proliferation Directors' Group on nuclear safety and security at the Zaporizhzhya Nuclear Power Plant","publisher":"Federal Foreign Office","publication_date":"2022-08-29","url":"https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/newsroom/news/zaporizhzhya-nuclear-power-plant-2548774","claim":"The G7 group said Russian control of Ukrainian nuclear facilities significantly raises the risk of a nuclear accident or incident and backed IAEA efforts to protect nuclear safety and security.","locator":"lines 101-102 in the opened page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary G7 statement with explicit nuclear-safety risk language and direct institutional remedy.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and highly relevant to catastrophic-risk management during the war.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Germany's government role in the G7 process, not to a unilateral Scholz action.","contrary_evidence":["This addresses a Russian-created risk environment more than a German choice.","It is a group statement, so Scholz's individual contribution is indirect."],"lenses":["1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Scholz, Biden agree Kremlin's nuclear threats 'irresponsible' in phonecall","publisher":"Reuters via Free Malaysia Today","publication_date":"2022-10-10","url":"https://www.freemalaysiatoday.com/category/world/2022/10/10/scholz-biden-agree-kremlins-nuclear-threats-irresponsible/","claim":"Scholz and Biden said Moscow's latest nuclear threats were irresponsible and would have exceptionally serious consequences, framing the response as escalation control rather than brinkmanship.","locator":"lead paragraph and quoted government statement","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on a contemporaneous Scholz-Biden call; strong evidence for crisis rhetoric and allied coordination.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 during the nuclear-threat phase of the Ukraine war.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Scholz's crisis messaging and alliance coordination.","contrary_evidence":["The call is about rhetoric and alliance signaling, not a concrete treaty or force-control decision.","It remains a mediated report rather than a verbatim transcript."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Scholz: Xi opposing nuclear weapons in Ukraine reason enough to visit China","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-11-05","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/scholz-xi-opposing-nuclear-weapons-in-ukraine-reason-enough-to-visit-china-2933708","claim":"After visiting Beijing, Scholz said the joint rejection of nuclear weapons use in Ukraine was reason enough for the trip, and the readout said Germany and China jointly opposed the use or threat of nuclear weapons.","locator":"lead paragraph and article summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on a contemporaneous diplomatic statement; strong for risk-reduction rhetoric and external coordination.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to global nuclear-risk signaling.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz diplomacy, though the substantive statement was joint with Xi and therefore partly shared.","contrary_evidence":["A joint statement with China is signaling, not binding arms control.","China's agreement was limited and did not amount to policy convergence on Russia."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Annual Disarmament Report","publisher":"Federal Foreign Office","publication_date":"2023-04-26","url":"https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/aussenpolitik/themen/disarmament-report-2022-2594380","claim":"The German government said that after 24 February 2022 Moscow repeatedly issued irresponsible nuclear threats, and that Germany worked in 2022 on cyber policy, lethal autonomous weapons, and a pledge against destructive anti-satellite tests.","locator":"lines 112-117 in the opened page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official retrospective report summarizing 2022 policy and threat environment; strong for end-of-year context.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Retrospective but directly about 2022 conduct and threat environment.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level attribution under Scholz; not an individual speech act.","contrary_evidence":["Retrospective summaries can smooth over intra-government disagreement.","Not all items are personally Scholz-directed."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Germany's support for nuclear sharing is vital to protect peace and freedom","publisher":"NATO","publication_date":"2020-05-11","url":"https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/events/transcripts/2020/05/11/germanys-support-for-nuclear-sharing-is-vital-to-protect-peace-and-freedom","claim":"NATO said Germany has long contributed dual-capable aircraft to nuclear sharing, and that the arrangement supports nonproliferation by reducing the incentive for states to seek their own nuclear weapons.","locator":"lines 825-829 in the opened page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official NATO transcript; useful inherited-baseline context, though not a 2022 Scholz action." ,"final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited baseline for Germany's 2022 nuclear posture rather than in-period conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Germany's NATO role and inherited posture, not solely to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["The transcript predates Scholz's chancellorship.","It describes alliance doctrine, not Germany-specific 2022 decision-making."],"lenses":["1B.6","1B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across these buckets:
- German authority and constraint pages: Chancellor biography, Chancellor duties, Basic Law Art. 65, Bundestag chancellor election, Bundestag constructive no-confidence explainer.
- Scholz 2022 security speeches and transcripts: 27 February policy statement, later federal-government summaries, Bundestag/official archive pages, and the March 2022 no-fly-zone interview.
- Arms-control and nuclear-risk sources: NPDI statement, G7 Zaporizhzhya statement, 2022 Annual Disarmament Report, NATO nuclear-sharing pages, NATO strategic-concept pages, and the NATO nuclear-sharing transcript.
- Reuters and Reuters-syndicated reporting: 11 February pre-invasion warning, 14 March F-35 decision, 7 April Ukraine guarantees, 9/10 October nuclear-threat response, 4/5 November China trip and joint nuclear statement, and a few redundant March/May/November follow-ups.
- Independent German-language coverage: ZEIT and Reuters-syndicated Euronews reports.

Main removals:
- Later 2023-2026 retrospectives and official summaries that were useful for orientation but not direct 2022 evidence were treated as context only or rejected as out-of-period for the core chapter record.
- Several Reuters pieces on adjacent Ukraine policy, sanctions, or defense aid were rejected as redundant once the no-fly-zone interview, the 27 February speech, and the F-35 procurement article were retained.
- General NATO doctrine pages were mostly rejected as background unless they directly supported Germany's inherited nuclear-sharing posture.
- Articles on Germany's civil nuclear power phase-out were excluded as off-topic for existential-risk responsibility under this chapter.
- Repeated coverage of the same October and November nuclear-threat episodes was deduplicated to one retained Reuters-sourced claim each.

**Remaining gaps**
- I still do not have internal German cabinet minutes or classified nuclear-planning records, so the exact depth of Scholz's personal involvement in NATO nuclear consultations remains indirect.
- The record on command-and-control discipline is mostly institutional and alliance-level; I did not find evidence of a specific Scholz-led reform to custody, safety, or alert posture.
- The biggest direct 2022 choices are rhetorical restraint, nuclear-sharing procurement, and arms-control signaling. I do not yet have a stronger source on whether those choices materially reduced risk beyond signaling.
- Scholz's role in cyber, AI, biological, or space-risk governance is only partially covered through the government's broader 2022 disarmament report, not through ruler-specific decisions.

If you want the next step, I can turn this into a chapter-ready evidence dossier with source IDs and lens mapping only, still without scoring.
